    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2590",
      "problem": "In the figure shown below, determine the measure of $\\angle EOA.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14176224/assets/80f47745a289bf021a4566a58d1961c93bb216e2df900b8effae8f2dda3f1606.png)",
      "worked_solution": "From the diagram, $\\angle COD$ is a right angle, so\n\n$$\nm\\angle COD = 90^\\circ.\n$$\n\nAlso, since $\\angle COD$ and $\\angle EOB$ are vertical angles, they have the same measure:\n\n$$\nm\\angle EOB=m\\angle COD=90^\\circ\n$$\n\nNow, since we know that $m\\angle AOB=40^{\\circ}$ and $m\\angle EOB = 90^\\circ,$ we can use the angle addition postulate to solve for $m\\angle EOA\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠EOA+m∠AOB & =m∠EOB \\\\ m∠EOA+{40}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠EOA & ={50}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
